name: Actual context drives scoped advisory ranking and read-only coverage recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/worklist_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: logs
submit: run worklist:rank
require-live-snap: 25 no ranked files | empty-ranking
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 40 context:build indexed | context-prepared
submit: run coverage:recommend {"limit":1}
require-live-snap: 25 recommendation(s) | recommendations
submit: run worklist:rank {"limit":1}
submit: worklist
require-live-snap: 25 1 of 4 ranked files shown | capped-ranking
expect: source freshness is unverified
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/worklist_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART capped
ask: Does real deterministic context produce advisory file ranking with visible evidence, an honest row cap and no claim that priority establishes a vulnerability or completes Map?
submit: logs
submit: run worklist:rank {"limit":4}
submit: worklist
require-live-snap: 25 4 of 4 ranked files shown | full-ranking
resize: 160x48
live-snap: worklist-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: worklist-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: worklist-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: worklist-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: worklist-reading-000-40x12
expect: RISK WORKLIST
expect: q back
keys: NPage
live-snap: worklist-reading-001-40x12
expect: RISK WORKLIST
expect: q back
